# Before starting

Welcome. Before starting or resuming work, check what `hostname` outputs.

- If it ends in "clank", {{ sandbox }}run whatever commands you need.
- Otherwise, stop and ask the user to edit this file.

# Environment

Your `Bash` tool uses zsh, not bash.

You're on NixOS {{ nixos_version }}; many things are installed, including:

{{ tools.join(", ") }}.

A prebuilt Linux binary downloaded by some tool can fail with a misleading ENOENT; patch for NixOS:

	patchelf --set-interpreter "$(patchelf --print-interpreter /bin/sh)" BIN

plus `--set-rpath` to a nix gcc-lib for libstdc++ if needed.

When waiting on something, generally don't use `sleep N` where N > 10; use the built-in task watching, or e.g. `wait-for-process-exit PID`, or loop something e.g. `rg -q PATTERN FILE` with a 2 second wait.

If git objects are broken: don't investigate, just try again in 7 seconds; if still broken: AskUserQuestion "Have you fixed it yet?" Y/N.

# Avoid consuming tokens in excess

Use `rg` in various ways until you know you need the rest of the file.

If you're Claude and are spending a lot of time in hairy / complex code, ask Astra via codex for help.

# The user isn't always right

{{ include "push_back.vto" }}

Don't assume the user really wants all the things that already exist; sometimes there are just odd leftovers.

So, treat the existing implementation as revisable. If it helps the design or keeps LOC down, redo it in a new file.

Always let the user know about any discovered opportunities for simplification.

If the user asks for more than one change, try doing and committing them separately (unless the changes are entwined).
{{ if node }}

# Working with Node projects

{{ if package_manager == "bun" }}
This project uses bun; avoid running npm or pnpm.
{{ else }}
npm sux; please use pnpm instead.
{{ /if }}
{{ /if }}
{{ if python }}

# Working with Python projects

Prefer `uv` and `uvx` over pip. A standalone script can use a PEP 723 `# /// script` block, for `uv run script.py`.
{{ /if }}

# There's plenty of time

If more external information is needed, think and keep iterating on web search queries to thoroughly check things. Tips: try site-specific searches e.g. site:github.com, reddit.com, news.ycombinator.com; try combinations of quoted items.

If you can't fetch something, use google-chrome or {{ curl_chrome }} on this machine.

# Tracking AI authorship

Files with any LLM-authored code (not counting mechanistic sed-like changes) begin with a comment like `// Model-output: <model name>`, one per model that contributed (e.g. "{{ claude_model }}", "{{ chatgpt_model }}"); keep existing lines.
